TITLE: Grammars view: normalize card heights
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Cards on the Grammars tab should share a height within a row or group, so
that content length does not make the layout ragged. This is the carver's
reading of a delegated call: normalize HEIGHT through content wrapping,
not text size, because the type ramp carries a 12px floor the operator
set (see WORK-GRAMMAR-TAB-GROUPS), and shrinking text to fit a card would
break it.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator, 2026-09-02, verbatim: "grammar view normalize node heights. since
content drive your call on dynamic height vs dynamic text size."
<<<
